  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As someone that mainly sticks to invite only instances with friends that I know are using specific mods to make their experience more accessible, then without an official modding API*, a stopgap would be to have an \"Enable EAC\" button when creating an instance and make it a player choice.\nIf unchecked, this could pop up a large warning message (\"this instance has Easy Anti Cheat disabled; other players may be able to do X, Y, and Z; VRChat Support cannot assist with technical issues encountered on this instance\", etc.) and require an interaction to confirm joining the instance even if \"skip go on load\" is checked.\n* I believe an API would be a better solution in terms of controlling what mods can do - and also, if there was a server side way of using and controlling them, that would solve the problem with support issues caused by mods since support staff would be able to see what mods are currently applied to an account.",
